/**
 * /faq/ —— 常见问题
 *
 * 覆盖两条产品线（Cart 与 Messaging）的**跨产品问题**。产品各自的细则留在各自页面
 * （Messaging 的计费细则在 `/messaging/pricing/`，Cart 的安装与恢复逻辑在 `/help/`）——
 * 本页只放「读者会先问的那一层」，避免同一答案在三个地方各写一遍然后漂移。
 *
 * 🔴 每条答案都必须能被代码或文档指认（取证位置见 `src/data/guides.js` 与
 *    `src/data/messagingPricing.js` 的文件头）。**禁写未核实数字**。
 *
 * 🔴 本页额外输出 FAQPage 结构化数据，用于搜索结果的展开。加问答时
 *    **必须同时加进 `FAQS` 数组**，结构化数据是从它生成的 —— 手写第二份 JSON-LD
 *    就会与页面正文漂移。
 *
 * @author 恒哥
 * @since 2026-10-12
 */
import React from 'react';
import { Link } from 'gatsby';
import Layout from '../components/Layout';
import SEO from '../components/SEO';
import { MESSAGING_PRODUCT_NAME, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../constants/brand';
import { INTEGRATION_STATS } from '../data/integrations';
import '../styles/marketing.css';

const FAQS = [
  {
    q: 'What does Whaleal actually build?',
    a: 'Two products. Whaleal Cart is a Shopify app that recovers abandoned checkouts. Whaleal Messaging is an orchestration layer that runs your messages over the CPaaS accounts you already hold \u2014 SMS, email and WhatsApp. They are separate products with separate pricing.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is a message orchestration layer?',
    a: 'It is the software above a provider account that decides which provider carries a message, at what rate, and what happened to it afterwards. It is not a provider itself: it holds no carrier accreditation, sells no message volume and appears on no provider invoice.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I have to move my Twilio (or Vonage, or Infobip) account to you?',
    a: 'No, and you cannot. You keep your account where it is and connect it using credentials you generate. Your numbers, your quota, your negotiated rate and your invoice all stay with your provider.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you charge per message?',
    a: 'No. Message charges are between you and your provider. The platform charges a flat subscription, and what varies between tiers is how many connections you can run, how fast you may submit, and how long delivery logs are kept.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I connect email or WhatsApp?',
    a: 'Yes. Both connect the same way as SMS — you link a provider account you already hold and send from the console. Delivery receipts come back normalized on every channel whose provider reports delivery (every SMS provider, Resend on email, Meta on WhatsApp); automatic failover between accounts and per-number pacing are SMS-channel features.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Why does the same text sometimes cost two messages?',
    a: 'SMS is billed per segment, and how much fits in a segment depends on the character set. GSM-7 fits 160 characters in a single segment; a message needing UCS-2 fits 70. Long messages are split into parts of 153 and 67 respectively, and each part is billed.',
  },
  {
    q: 'If someone replies STOP, are they really suppressed?',
    a: 'A recognized opt-out reply writes a suppression record for that address, and a check runs before each marketing send, so the address is not handed to the provider again. There is one caveat worth knowing: some providers handle opt-out at the carrier level, in which case the reply may never reach us as an inbound message at all.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can a recipient opt back in?',
    a: 'Yes. Replying START, YES or UNSTOP deactivates the suppression record and sends a confirmation. Note that this is a change in our records — on some sender types the carrier may also have blocked the number on its own side, and that has to be released separately.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is an accepted message a delivered message?',
    a: 'No. Acceptance means the provider took responsibility for the message. Delivery is a later, separate event that arrives as a receipt. Only the terminal outcome should be used to judge whether a message arrived.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do you store the content of my messages?',
    a: 'No. A delivery record holds the recipient, the provider, the status, the error code, the encoding and the segment count, plus a retention deadline. Message bodies are not stored on any plan.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How are my provider credentials protected?',
    a: 'They are encrypted at rest with AES-256-GCM and are not sent back to the browser after saving, where the console shows a fingerprint instead. The details are on the security page.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How many providers can I connect?',
    a: `Self-service connections to ${INTEGRATION_STATS.byChannel.SMS} SMS providers, ${INTEGRATION_STATS.byChannel.EMAIL} email providers and ${INTEGRATION_STATS.byChannel.WHATSAPP} WhatsApp providers today, plus a plan limit on how many connections you may run. Underneath the SMS channel sits an SMS adapter library of ${INTEGRATION_STATS.sdkAdapters} adapters; those outside the self-service set are unlocked on request rather than self-service.`,
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I get help?',
    a: 'Email us. It goes to the people who build the products, and including the account or shop you are asking about lets us look at the real records rather than guessing.',
  },
];

export default function FaqPage() {
  return (
    <Layout>
      {/* 🔴 FAQPage 结构化数据由 SEO 组件统一生成（2026-10-14 收口）。
          此前这段 JSON-LD 是在本文件里手写的，而 /features/、/industries/、/use-cases/、
          /compare/、/solutions/ 这些页**明明也在正文里渲染问答，却一条 schema 都没输出**。
          现在只要把数组传下去，生成逻辑只有一处，与正文同源 ⇒ 不可能漂移。 */}
      <SEO
        title="Frequently asked questions"
        description={`Straight answers about ${MESSAGING_PRODUCT_NAME} and Whaleal Cart: bring-your-own-account, per-message billing, SMS segments and opt-out handling.`}
        pathname="/faq/"
        softwareApp={false}
        faqs={FAQS}
        breadcrumbs={[
          { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
          { name: 'FAQ', path: '/faq/' },
        ]}
      />

      <div className="mk">
        <header className="mk-hero">
          <span className="mk-eyebrow">FAQ</span>
          <h1>Questions we actually get</h1>
          <p className="mk-lead">
            Short answers, with a link where a topic needs more room than a paragraph. If yours is
            not here, email works better than a form.
          </p>
        </header>

        <section className="mk-section">
          <dl className="mk-faq">
            {FAQS.map((f) => (
              <div className="mk-faq-item" key={f.q}>
                <dt>{f.q}</dt>
                <dd>{f.a}</dd>
              </div>
            ))}
          </dl>
        </section>

        <section className="mk-section">
          <h2>Still have a question?</h2>
          <p className="mk-section-lead">
            The guides go deeper on how the message channel behaves, and pricing details live with
            pricing. For anything else, email is the fastest route.
          </p>
          <div className="mk-actions">
            <Link className="mk-btn mk-btn-secondary" to="/guides/">
              Read the guides
            </Link>
            <Link className="mk-btn mk-btn-secondary" to="/messaging/pricing/">
              Messaging pricing
            </Link>
            <a className="mk-btn mk-btn-primary" href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>
              {SUPPORT_EMAIL}
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>
    </Layout>
  );
}
